**About this Project**

This project is implemented for practicing Software Testing skills by designing Automated Unit Test Cases, along with manual tests. 

The focus of the project is on testing the methods of ArrayList class in the Java Standard Edition Library. Each method has been covered for the creation of Unit Test Cases. Including testing the basic functionality where elements are added, removed, retrieved, the size of the ArrayList is measured and the index of specific elements in the list are found. 

The entire automation of the ArrayList testing uses Automation Test Tool like JUnit for Java and Pex (--------------------            Assert.IsTrue(New_Ret <= Old_arrListCount);

		 // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ New array list's index of x == old array list index of x  
            Assert.AreEqual((Old_arrListContainsX ? Old_arrListLastIndexOfX : -1), New_Ret);

		 // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ New array list's count is same as old arrays count 
            Assert.AreEqual(Old_arrListCount, New_arrListCount);

		 // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ New array list's last index of x is <= old array list's last index of x  
            Assert.IsTrue(New_arrListLastOfX <= Old_arrListLastIndexOfX);

		 // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ For x in the array list and for last occurrence, new array list's contains is true  
            Assert.IsTrue(New_arrListContainsX);
        }
